.\" A sample man page for rs-rich-ext's document tests.
.TH GREET 1 "October 2026" "greet 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
greet \- print a friendly greeting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B greet
[\fB\-n\fR \fIcount\fR]
[\fB\-\-shout\fR]
.IR name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B greet
writes a greeting for each
.I name
to standard output.
The greeting is \(lqHello\(rq unless
.B \-\-shout
says otherwise \(em then it is louder.
.SS Options
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-count =\fIN\fR
Repeat each greeting
.I N
times.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-shout\fR
Write the greeting in capitals.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Works with every name.
.IP \(bu 2
Ignores the locale.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ greet \-n 2 world
Hello, world
Hello, world
.EE
.SH FILES
.TS
tab(;);
lb lb
l l.
Path;Purpose
_
~/.greetrc;User settings
/etc/greetrc;System settings
.TE
